WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.730 --> 00:00:01.563
- Look at that.

00:00:01.563 --> 00:00:03.920
(audience applauding)

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:05.303
- [Jay] Very nice.

00:00:05.303 --> 00:00:06.210
- Thank you, Jay.

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.980
I went Christmas for you, today.

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:10.525
- I can see you look like a
baked potato wrapped in foil.

00:00:10.525 --> 00:00:12.251
(Kristin laughing)

00:00:12.251 --> 00:00:13.200
- That was funny.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.103
- No, that's cute.

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:17.321
And the boots that go with it, very nice.

00:00:17.321 --> 00:00:18.154
- I mean, you know what?

00:00:18.154 --> 00:00:19.670
Here's to the women out there,

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:21.870
you don't always have to spend a fortune.

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:23.140
These are Steve Madden.

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:24.100
I know you don't care,

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:27.470
and I'm glad you don't know the brand.

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:29.680
But these were not expensive.

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:31.573
- No, and I have to say.

00:00:32.567 --> 00:00:34.610
You are right on both counts.

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:36.910
I don't care and I don't
know the brand, yeah.

00:00:38.411 --> 00:00:41.053
- And if we were dating,
I would be very relieved.

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:45.570
- If we were dating, I would
be in a lot of trouble.

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:47.667
So let's just leave it at that.

00:00:47.667 --> 00:00:49.500
And I saw you sang with Kelly in New York

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:51.270
during a season premiere.

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:52.559
That's very cool.

00:00:52.559 --> 00:00:55.620
(audience applauding)

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:57.830
- She picked a song, Jay
"On Top Of The World"

00:00:57.830 --> 00:00:59.890
that hardly anybody would ever pick.

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:03.990
And it was really hot
for some reason that day.

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:05.820
And I showed up in three-inch heels

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:07.090
and she had her Converse on

00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:09.230
and she's like, "We're
just gonna walk down."

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:11.010
And there was hot dogs sellers

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:13.600
and people taking our
pictures and we're singing.

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:15.030
She's like, "Just ignore them.

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:16.200
Just ignore them."

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:17.850
And we just had the best time.

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:18.958
I'm proud of her.

00:01:18.958 --> 00:01:20.880
I'm proud of her.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.273
- Well, let me ask you this.

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:25.630
How excited are you that Broadway is back?

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:28.110
That's your life, that's
where you come from.

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:31.510
- Well, anything with a live
audience, Jay, and you know.

00:01:31.510 --> 00:01:34.011
It's been like having you all here today.

00:01:34.011 --> 00:01:37.637
(audience applauding)

00:01:37.637 --> 00:01:41.470
- I saw her live show
at the Disney Theater

00:01:41.470 --> 00:01:44.550
and it was really just an amazing shift

00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:46.380
because there's so many tricks on TV.

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:49.380
You know, they add sound
and they mix things in,

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:51.490
but to see somebody with pure voice

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:52.460
just come out and sing.

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:54.610
It really was an amazing evening.

00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:55.669
It really was.
- Thank you.

00:01:55.669 --> 00:01:57.141
- I really enjoyed it,
I really enjoyed it.

00:01:57.141 --> 00:01:59.500
Now, tell me about this.

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:02.175
You're gonna play Dolly
Parton in a musical?

00:02:02.175 --> 00:02:04.330
- Well, I want to,

00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:05.480
I'm lacking a couple things

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:07.590
and I think we both know what they are.

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:08.613
- I didn't say it.

00:02:09.650 --> 00:02:10.540
- He didn't say it.

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:13.430
Now, she has said before
in the past several times

00:02:13.430 --> 00:02:16.540
that she does see me as
someone who could play her,

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:19.410
and I just wanna say,
"Dolly, where's the camera?

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:20.730
Where's my camera?

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:23.550
Dolly, hurry up.

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:25.330
I'm ready."

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:26.523
- I think that would be, yeah.

00:02:26.523 --> 00:02:28.700
I mean, you could obviously
have the voice for it.

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:29.570
Yeah, you can sing.

00:02:29.570 --> 00:02:31.640
- I just grew up listening
to her and you know,

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:34.899
I do a pretty good, like I just,

00:02:34.899 --> 00:02:37.193
♪ Here you come again ♪

00:02:37.193 --> 00:02:38.657
That's my favorite.

00:02:38.657 --> 00:02:42.093
- I'm thinking, I gotta go with "Jolene".

00:02:42.093 --> 00:02:45.414
♪ Jolene, Jolene, Jolene ♪

00:02:45.414 --> 00:02:47.511
I mean, come on, I can play Dolly.

00:02:47.511 --> 00:02:50.940
(audience applauding)

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:52.320
- I remember seeing Dolly Parton,

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:55.170
nobody else would know
this, on candid camera

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:56.040
when she was very young.

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:57.850
- I remember Kenny.

00:02:57.850 --> 00:03:00.560
- But Dolly Parton, she
was just a young girl,

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:03.067
but she would stand on the street corner.

00:03:03.067 --> 00:03:04.760
"Could someone carry
me across this puddle?"

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:05.930
There's a puddle of water

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:07.380
and guys would come and pick her up

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:08.310
and carry her across them.

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:09.220
It was like the funniest.

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:10.790
You should ask her about that when you do.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:12.326
I'm sure she's forgotten about it.

00:03:12.326 --> 00:03:13.800
- She's so smart.

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:15.540
- Now, are you gonna
move to Nashville now?

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:16.410
Is that what I hear?

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:19.980
- Actually, I'm gonna
keep my place in New York.

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:23.370
I'll never not be a new
Yorker, Jay, but I am moving.

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:25.060
I've actually bought a place in Nashville.

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:26.580
I just wanna go.

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:27.520
I love it there.

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:29.660
You know, I just love it
there, it feels like home.

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:31.829
- We gotta talk about "The Voice"

00:03:31.829 --> 00:03:33.450
because this is Kelly's show.

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:35.970
Now, you're an advisor on the show,

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:39.697
but you were working
against Kelly, is that true?

00:03:39.697 --> 00:03:42.010
(booing)

00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:43.765
- That is a fact.

00:03:43.765 --> 00:03:46.394
(booing)

00:03:46.394 --> 00:03:49.510
I feel like I need to take
a shower now, thanks a lot.

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:54.300
Ariana Grande, I've known
since she was 10 years old

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:58.940
and she called and asked
if I would be her advisor

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:00.320
and we had been staying very close

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:01.170
and I said yes.

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:03.020
But besides Kelly's team,

00:04:03.020 --> 00:04:05.307
I think Ariana's team is very good.

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:07.713
- Wow.

00:04:07.713 --> 00:04:08.651
There you go.

00:04:08.651 --> 00:04:11.197
(audience clapping)

00:04:11.197 --> 00:04:14.200
Did you guys, you and Ariana
used to go on double dates?

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:15.033
Is that true?

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:20.290
- We had some, well, not as a couple,

00:04:20.290 --> 00:04:21.227
which there's nothing wrong with that,

00:04:21.227 --> 00:04:24.070
but no, with other partners.

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:26.120
Yeah, we had some dates, yeah.

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:27.320
- But not when she was 10.

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:28.153
- No.

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:30.430
Then I'd be in jail.

00:04:30.430 --> 00:04:31.737
- That's right, you got to.

00:04:31.737 --> 00:04:34.320
- But we just go and we like bowling.

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:36.805
We like truffle pizza
from Craig's here in LA.

00:04:36.805 --> 00:04:38.300
Have you ever tried truffle pizza?

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:39.880
- [Jay] What kind of pizza?

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:41.298
- [Kristin] The truffle pizza.

00:04:41.298 --> 00:04:42.667
- Okay. All right there, I don't care.

00:04:42.667 --> 00:04:43.500
- [Kristin] Have you had it?

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:45.250
- No, I haven't.

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:48.033
In my family, I'd be beaten
if I had a truffle pizza.

00:04:49.442 --> 00:04:51.060
It's like pineapple on a pizza.

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:51.893
- I agree.

00:04:51.893 --> 00:04:53.598
But no, you're wrong on this.

00:04:53.598 --> 00:04:55.223
Just, will you trust me?

00:04:55.223 --> 00:04:57.630
Will you trust me, Jay?

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:59.560
- Cheap Italian food is the best in time.

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:00.810
Why do you put truffles on it

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:03.003
and some pig going (snorting) on my pizza?

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:05.768
No, it doesn't.

00:05:05.768 --> 00:05:07.005
- [Kristin] It's yum.

00:05:07.005 --> 00:05:07.838
- It's all right.

00:05:07.838 --> 00:05:08.671
- You're missing out.

00:05:08.671 --> 00:05:10.510
- Right. Now, what can we expect
on the new Christmas album?

00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:11.343
Tell me about it.

00:05:11.343 --> 00:05:12.640
- When I was thinking about,

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:14.810
'cause doesn't it feel
like Christmas was canceled

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:16.538
for like two years or something?

00:05:16.538 --> 00:05:17.660
- [Jay] Yeah, it does.

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:19.490
- I was pretty down in the dumps

00:05:19.490 --> 00:05:20.870
and not being able to perform live,

00:05:20.870 --> 00:05:22.910
but doing other kinds of
work that I also enjoy,

00:05:22.910 --> 00:05:24.590
but I like a live crowd.

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:25.423
And so.

00:05:26.516 --> 00:05:30.077
(audience applauding)

00:05:30.077 --> 00:05:31.450
- You were just booing her a minute ago.

00:05:31.450 --> 00:05:32.800
What a bunch of hypocrites.

00:05:34.670 --> 00:05:36.120
- What are you doing to them?

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:40.780
I was thinking about
the feel for the album

00:05:40.780 --> 00:05:42.660
and I went to Nashville to record it

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:43.750
with some of the best musicians.

00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:46.340
And we had partitions,
and we had our masks,

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:48.710
and I said, "It's we are light.

00:05:48.710 --> 00:05:50.100
We are light for each other.

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:52.620
We see the light coming
at the end of the tunnel."

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:55.428
And I have Keb' Mo' on there doing,

00:05:55.428 --> 00:05:57.540
"How Dare I Do a Blues Song?"

00:05:57.540 --> 00:05:59.290
We're doing "Merry Christmas Baby".

00:06:02.027 --> 00:06:03.250
A lot of songs y'all know.

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:04.730
And then a couple that aren't,

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:06.987
there's a song on there I co-wrote called

00:06:06.987 --> 00:06:09.187
"Santa, I Got A Bone To Pick With You".

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:12.740
It's about the crappy presents
you get for Christmas.

00:06:12.740 --> 00:06:13.790
- Really?

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:16.283
Well, that's I think the
real meaning of Christmas.

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:18.949
Complaining about the crappy gifts

00:06:18.949 --> 00:06:22.770
that someone took a lot of
love and time just to look for.

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:26.140
- I mean, contacts, mismatched socks?

00:06:26.140 --> 00:06:28.580
It happened to me.

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:30.990
- Now you have a song and this one.

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:31.944
Was it "Why Can't Christmas?"

00:06:31.944 --> 00:06:33.297
- "Why Can't It Be Christmas Every Day?"

00:06:33.297 --> 00:06:35.810
"Why Can't It Be Christmas
Every Freaking Day?"

00:06:35.810 --> 00:06:38.620
- But that wouldn't work.

00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:39.940
Then you need another holiday.

00:06:39.940 --> 00:06:41.190
You need super Christmas.

00:06:42.030 --> 00:06:42.863
It's like champagne.

00:06:42.863 --> 00:06:45.440
If you drink it every
day, you're an alcoholic.

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:47.420
You know, it's like a special occasion.

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:48.253
- You telling me

00:06:48.253 --> 00:06:49.870
you'd be tired of
Christmas every single day,

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:51.890
getting presents and going
to see all your family.

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:54.830
- I'd be tired buying
presents every single day.

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:56.120
Guys, buy present.

00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:57.832
Guys, is that pretty much what it is?

00:06:57.832 --> 00:06:59.203
Thank you very much, thank you very much.

00:07:00.170 --> 00:07:02.173
It's bad enough we got Valentine's Day.

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:05.720
Somehow the wool got pulled
over our eyes on that one,

00:07:05.720 --> 00:07:07.670
middle of February I need to gift wife.

00:07:09.550 --> 00:07:12.782
So no, Christmas every day
would be a nightmare, oh my God.

00:07:12.782 --> 00:07:15.453
- A gift can be just
something like a smile.

00:07:16.292 --> 00:07:17.530
(audience awwing)

00:07:17.530 --> 00:07:22.257
- Guys, guys, I'll give
you props for that one.

00:07:22.257 --> 00:07:26.510
A friend of mine for his
25th wedding anniversary

00:07:26.510 --> 00:07:28.270
he told me, I said, "Well,
what did you get her?"

00:07:28.270 --> 00:07:29.570
He said, "I got her a breadmaker."

00:07:29.570 --> 00:07:31.790
I go, "Okay, first of all,

00:07:31.790 --> 00:07:33.090
you don't give your wife a breadmaker.

00:07:33.090 --> 00:07:35.850
Why don't you give her
a broom or a vacuum?"

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:38.180
He goes, "I think you're crazy."

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:40.717
And then she starts to
open it and she goes,

00:07:40.717 --> 00:07:41.720
"Is this a joke?"

00:07:41.720 --> 00:07:43.050
He goes, "Yeah, you're right.

00:07:43.050 --> 00:07:44.550
You're like, you have to suck.

00:07:45.469 --> 00:07:47.690
Luckily he thought fast.

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:51.460
It was late comments
so I got this as a gag

00:07:51.460 --> 00:07:53.200
and he managed to avoid the bullet.

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:54.033
But then he said-

00:07:54.033 --> 00:07:55.280
- In two days you get a new car.

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:56.820
- That's right, that's right.

00:07:56.820 --> 00:07:58.470
And that's literally what it took.

00:07:58.470 --> 00:08:00.923
So don't give me a smile, shut up.

00:08:02.450 --> 00:08:04.290
Just a smile, yeah.

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:07.740
Now what holiday traditions
do you have back in Oklahoma?

00:08:07.740 --> 00:08:09.790
- Well, we eat, and then we eat-

00:08:09.790 --> 00:08:10.623
- [Jay] Really? Eating?

00:08:10.623 --> 00:08:12.207
- And then we eat some more.

00:08:12.207 --> 00:08:13.182
- There you go.

00:08:13.182 --> 00:08:16.013
- And then we pray and then we eat.

00:08:16.013 --> 00:08:18.461
And we pray about all
the food we've eaten.

00:08:18.461 --> 00:08:21.988
(audience applauding)

00:08:21.988 --> 00:08:24.990
- I mean, are there any sort
of real Oklahoma traditions

00:08:24.990 --> 00:08:25.823
that you have?

00:08:25.823 --> 00:08:28.930
- I mean, my dad, there's
a channel with one.

00:08:28.930 --> 00:08:29.763
- [Jay] What is that?

00:08:29.763 --> 00:08:31.320
- He always goes, "Now this year,

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:32.320
we're going to go around the table,

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:34.190
we're gonna tell everybody
what we're most grateful for."

00:08:34.190 --> 00:08:36.890
I'm like, "Okay, you first."

00:08:36.890 --> 00:08:39.083
Because he doesn't like to cry.

00:08:39.980 --> 00:08:44.177
And so he'll go, "Well,
I'm most, excuse me."

00:08:45.240 --> 00:08:48.047
I'm most (mumbling)

00:08:48.047 --> 00:08:50.523
and I just liked to watch him suffer.

00:08:51.930 --> 00:08:54.330
- Well, you really have
the spirit of Christmas.

00:08:55.980 --> 00:08:59.150
Now speaking of Oklahoma,
I have to ask about this.

00:08:59.150 --> 00:09:01.750
Tell me about this throwback
cheerleading photo.

00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:02.734
Can we put that up there?

00:09:02.734 --> 00:09:03.630
- [Kristin] Which one?

00:09:03.630 --> 00:09:04.463
- Where is it?

00:09:04.463 --> 00:09:06.682
There it is, there it is right there.

00:09:06.682 --> 00:09:09.849
(audience applauding)

00:09:14.894 --> 00:09:15.727
I got to ask,

00:09:15.727 --> 00:09:17.450
how many 40-year-olds
are still in high school?

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:18.500
Look at that picture.

00:09:19.460 --> 00:09:23.210
- I'm so upset by my hairdo.

00:09:23.210 --> 00:09:25.360
And by the way, the
pompoms when I was young

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:26.193
were as big as me.

00:09:26.193 --> 00:09:30.460
And I remember having to do
a tick check after that, Jay.

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:31.293
- [Jay] A tick check?

00:09:31.293 --> 00:09:34.400
- Around the woods, my hair, my hair.

00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:37.333
- I thought there was some
dead animal at your feet.

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:41.860
It looks like some dead zebra hybrid.

00:09:41.860 --> 00:09:44.092
- No, you mean The Tigers?

00:09:44.092 --> 00:09:46.210
- I mean, what is it about old?

00:09:46.210 --> 00:09:48.100
Why do people look older in old photos?

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:51.660
- Because, are we not always
trying to look older y'all?

00:09:51.660 --> 00:09:52.990
And then when you get to be about 30,

00:09:52.990 --> 00:09:54.840
you're like, "Let's stop that train."

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:57.767
- But it's going too fast.

00:09:57.767 --> 00:09:59.550
- But it's going too fast.

00:09:59.550 --> 00:10:01.743
Oh my hair, let's never show that again.

